OL,3,GNEWSATudor silver spoon to go under the
OL,4,Ahammer
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 450-year-old silver spoon made during
OL,7,Fthe reign of Elizabeth I is set to be
OL,8,Fauctioned.
OL,10,FThe Tudor relic, made in Chester, is
OL,11,Festimated to fetch between
OL,12,F#2,000`#3,000 when it goes under the
OL,13,Fhammer at Roseberys, London, on 30
OL,14,FSeptember.
OL,16,FThe relic is believed to be one of the
OL,17,Fearliest known surviving Chester silver
OL,18,Fspoons. The only comparably early
OL,19,Fexample identified is a c.1580 spoon by
OL,20,FWilliam Mutton in the Grosvenor Museum
OL,21,Fin Chester, the auctioneers said.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
